message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a **rotating card** that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: content inside the card */
.card-content {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide back side while rotating */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>Hover over this card to see it rotate!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` sets a perspective so the 3D rotation looks realistic.
2. **Transform style** – `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space.
3. **Transition** – `transition: transform 0.6s ease` makes the rotation smooth.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis.
5. **Backface visibility** – Hides the backside of the card during rotation (optional if you add more content).

You can replace the gradient, size, or content with whatever fits your design. Enjoy!
